'''apprehensively''' (ap-rẹ̄-hen′siv-li), ''adv.'' In an apprehensive manner; with apprehension.

'''apprehensiveness''' (ap-rẹ̄-hen′siv-nes), ''n.'' The state or quality of being apprehensive. (''a'') Readiness to understand. (''b'') Fearfulness.

